course: dictionary
lesson: 8460
title: Salamanders: amphibians with a tail
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A salamander is an amphibian, a group that includes frogs, toads and newts. «Frogs, toads, newts and salamanders are amphibians; snakes, lizards, crocodiles and turtles are reptiles.» Reptiles have dry, scaly skin, so skin is one clue for telling the groups apart.
explain: A salamander can look a bit like a lizard, with a long body, a tail and four short legs. But its skin is smooth and damp, not dry and scaly. When you meet a new animal, check the clues in the words around it: damp skin and a tail point to a salamander.
explain: Some words come from old stories. In legends, a salamander was a creature that could live in fire. Read the word «legend» as a clue: this is a story belief, not a fact about real animals.
fact: A salamander is a small amphibian with a long body, a tail, four short legs and smooth, damp skin.
fact: «The fire salamander lives in damp forests», and its bright colours warn that its skin is poisonous.
fact: Some salamanders can regrow a lost tail or leg.
fact: The axolotl keeps its baby gills, the feathery frills on its head, and stays in water all its life.
fact: The old belief that a salamander could live in fire probably came from salamanders crawling out of logs thrown on a fire.
exercise: What is a salamander? | A reptile with dry, scaly skin | A bird that cannot fly | *A small amphibian with smooth, damp skin
exercise: «The fire salamander's bright colours warn of poisonous skin.» What do the bright colours do? | They make it lighter to carry | *They warn that its skin is poisonous | They help it fly
exercise: Which animal can regrow a lost tail? | A snake | A crocodile | A turtle | *A salamander
test: In old stories, what was a salamander? | A large snake that lived under the sea | A bird that sang in the rain | *A creature that could live in fire
test: «The axolotl keeps its baby gills.» Which feature is a baby feature that it keeps? | Its hard shell | Its long legs | Its wings | *Its feathery gills
exam: Which two groups do salamanders belong to? | Mammals | Fish | *Amphibians | Reptiles
